<%- /*
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Lusoris <lusoris@pm.me>
SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2

Caller of the shared release fan-out, kept beside the merge train caller
in the fleet's operations repository as
.github/workflows/merge-train-release.yml.
The steps live in .github/workflows/merge-train-release.yml of the shared
repository, named by commit (decision record 0098).

Runner: a runner with python3. Set .RunnerTag independently of the train
caller when release legs should use a separate runner set.

Scopes: GITHUB_TOKEN gets actions: read only, to read the train run and its artifact.
Release legs use repository-limited app tokens. The merge-train environment
holds MERGE_TRAIN_APP_KEY; MERGE_TRAIN_APP_CLIENT_ID holds the app's client id,
as described by templates/callers/merge-train.yml.tmpl.

Trigger: the train job's workflow_dispatch with its run id, including failed
sweeps with a nonempty release list. An empty list dispatches nothing.
A person with write access may dispatch by hand
with a train run id. The plan checks that run's workflow path, event, branch,
repository, status and conclusion.
No workflow-level concurrency on purpose: queued release legs must not hold
the train. The reusable workflow serializes each repository's legs across runs.

Required check: none; never a pull request check (cordanaLLM/praetor#1212).
Fields: .Shared.Repository, .Shared.Commit, .Shared.Version and .RunnerTag
are supplied by the template renderer (cordanaLLM/praetor#1211).

Licence header: the rendered caller starts with the consumer's own header,
written from .Licence. Empty notes inside the fields keep this repository's
licence check from reading the template lines as tags.
*/ -%>
# SPDX-<%/* */%>FileCopyrightText: <% .Licence.CopyrightText %>
# SPDX-<%/* */%>License-Identifier: <% .Licence.Identifier %>
---
name: Merge train releases

on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      train_run_id:
        description: Train run whose release list is read.
        type: string
        required: true

      artifact_id:
        description: Set by the train; empty for a request by hand.
        type: string
        required: false
        default: ""

permissions: {}

jobs:
  release:
    name: Merge train releases
    permissions:
      actions: read # the plan reads the train run and downloads its release list artifact
    uses: <% .Shared.Repository %>/.github/workflows/merge-train-release.yml@<% .Shared.Commit %> # <% .Shared.Version %>
    with:
      train_run_id: ${{ inputs.train_run_id }}
      artifact_id: ${{ inputs.artifact_id }}
      runner: <% .RunnerTag %>
      app_client_id: ${{ vars.MERGE_TRAIN_APP_CLIENT_ID }}
    secrets:
      app_private_key: ${{ secrets.MERGE_TRAIN_APP_KEY }}
